WEBVTT

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.480
Hey, guys! I've gathered some dry branches!

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.930
Great! Good work!

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.980
Welcome back, Mile-chan.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.870
We've finished setting up camp here.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.580
Hey, guys. I know we're close to town, 
but this is a little too relaxed.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.110
Don't worry about it!

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.440
There's nothing that will pop up 
around here that we can't defeat.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.210
And with your search magic, Mile, 
they can't take us by surprise, either.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.670
It's true. With you here, Mile-chan, 
we don't have anything to fear.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.200
It's kinda cold, don't you think?

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.880
Mile! Bring out a blanket!

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.890
Oh. Can I have one, too?

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.870
I'd like one as well, please.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.510
Did Doraem—

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.010
—feel like this too, I wonder.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.020
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.030
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.030
<b>Didn't I Say Arrogance Leads to Trouble?!</b>

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.560
They're the ones we've heard about.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.790
Wow! Isn't that Mile-sama?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:05.780
They're so awesome.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.870
I heard they took down a wyvern.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:08.800
Do you think it's all true?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.150
I feel like everyone's looking this way.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.290
What? You hadn't noticed?

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.920
Not long ago, we became the center 
of attention here at the Guild.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:20.800
What? Why?

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.680
A certain party's been doing far better 
than expected for rookies since its debut,

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.810
and now, they've gone and successfully 
taken down a wyvern. That's why.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:29.930
I see.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:39.110
With that, we exceeded the Guild's 
expectations of rookies,

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.780
and now they're starting 
to see us as future aces.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.990
I see. So that's what's going on.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:45.990
Which is why...

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.750
We're going to take on even bigger quests,

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:52.460
and elevate the name "The Crimson Vow,"
 as well as our Hunter ranks!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:57.340
Once we have higher ranks, we'll be able to 
take on even more profitable quests, after all.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.580
That's true.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.150
U-Um...

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.590
How about this one?

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:04.860
A search for an investigation 
team that went into the forest

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.970
on an inquiry and went missing, huh?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:10.680
It looks like the completion reward 
has been overwritten several times.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.280
That means that other groups 
have tried and failed,

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.490
and the rewards been increased accordingly.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:19.960
Sounds like fun! Let's take this quest.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.440
Um, just a minute—

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.490
—bita-kun.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.510
Bita-kun?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.160
Who's that?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.670
Um, I was hoping I could hang back a 
little on backing everyone up this time.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.300
Huh?

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.250
Why?

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:39.200
Lately, I've been thinking that everyone 
depends on me a little too much.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:44.010
At this rate, the moment I leave,
 the party will collapse.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.870
Leave?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.170
Wait. Mile?

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.260
Are you planning to leave the party?

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.910
That's not what I mean.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.270
Illness, accidents...

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.370
There's no way to predict the 
timing of a person's death.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.950
What are you talking about?

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.480
You're overthinking things.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.760
No, I'm not.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.870
When the moment of death arrives, you die.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.990
Truly. Just like that.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.230
Well, that aside...

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.430
Lately, I've been thinking that 
we've been relying on Mile too much.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.210
You can scale down the backup.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.200
Then, with that in mind,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.960
please reconsider whether we want to 
take on that quest you were discussing.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.270
Under these circumstances, 
it might be be a little rough.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.720
Yes, it might.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.150
Should we consider a different quest?

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.810
No. We'll take it.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.200
What?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.290
If we back down here,

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.830
it's like we're admitting we can't 
do anything without you, isn't it?

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:40.940
That's true.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.960
I didn't mean that I think 
you can't do anything...

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:44.940
We'll take it!

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.200
We'll take it!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.670
I see.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.250
You want this quest?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:56.410
Yes!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.440
Hey! They said they're taking that quest!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.630
That's insane!

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:05.090
I see. Well, you girls might just 
manage to resolve the situation.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.050
In that case, allow me to explain 
the details of the quest.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:13.760
For a while now, there's been something 
strange about the monsters of the forest.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.660
Monsters that should be 
easy to find aren't there.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.080
Monsters appear where they shouldn't be.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.800
The Guild wanted to investigate 
the cause of the phenomena,

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.000
so they brought together a scholar 
and Hunters to guard them,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.280
and formed an investigation team.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.450
It's that team that's gone missing.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.940
The quest is to find them.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.620
At this point, I don't see 
anything out of the ordinary.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.600
Should I use search magic?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.520
No. We're still okay.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.500
We have to show you what we can do this
without depending on you, right?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.120
But this quest seems pretty tough, so...

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.560
Godspeed Sword! 1.2x speed!

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.490
Water Ball! Ultra Hot!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.370
Flame Sphere!

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:35.190
Pauline-san, Reina-san, when did 
you learn to use that new magic?

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:40.880
And, Mavis-san, wasn't that 
Godspeed Sword faster than 1.2x speed?

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.000
No. It was 1.2x speed.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.720
But since I've continued to train, 
my base abilities have increased,

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.510
so I might have gotten a little faster,
 and a little stronger.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.130
It was quite surprising.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.380
Being overly dependent on you was wrong of us,

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.330
but we have been keeping 
up our regular training.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.080
Have you? I'm glad.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.210
Can you die peacefully now?

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:03.290
Yes!

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.140
Please don't say "yes" like that.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.950
Since Mile is saying that, 
she'll outlive us all.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:11.960
That's right.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.910
She'll be a wrinkly old woman,

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.670
gathering up the children and 
telling them Altered Folktales.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.180
Oh! I can just picture it!

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.560
You think so?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.000
Of course.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:27.060
Things do seem strange here.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.440
The deeper we go into the forest,

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.920
the fewer small animals 
and small monsters we see.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.450
And now, the stronger, 
mid-size and larger monsters

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.700
seem to have come out of the deeper areas.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.940
What we can deduce from this is...

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:43.520
That the monsters' territories 
have suddenly changed... Right?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:44.320
Right.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.130
A powerful creature has appeared.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.210
Or a creature's incursion has caused 
the sudden change in the habitat.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:54.590
It could be that a monster of earth dragon
 or fenrir-class has appeared.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:55.380
Right?

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.290
Looks like it got away.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.930
I thought I'd be able to hit it.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.290
The fact that it was able 
to dodge means that

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.010
it's highly intelligent and 
has very good reflexes.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:12.320
So, in addition to being 
earth dragon or fenrir-class,

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.480
it's also a skilled observer.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:17.300
It might be difficult for us 
to handle this on our own.

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:21.440
We should head back and form 
a large-scale search party.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:22.800
Um...

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.790
Can we search just a little longer?

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.990
The investigation team is lost out there 
in the woods, in this dangerous situation.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.360
We need to find them as quickly as possible.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:36.750
And in the worst case scenario,
 if I go all out,

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.800
I think I should be able to fight an 
earth dragon or fenrir-class monster.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.340
You're probably right, but...

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.560
All right. Change of plan, then.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.940
Starting now, we stick to Mile and 
have her help with everything.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.060
Okay!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:53.270
Of course, we'll do everything we can, too.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:53.950
Right!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.280
There aren't any creatures 
in the area likely to attack.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.370
Forget attacking. I can't even 
hear any animal cries at all.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.650
And we haven't seen any mid-size 
or larger monsters around, either.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.440
Do you think it means we're getting closer to

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.880
whatever's causing the strange 
phenomena in the forest?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.930
Mavis-san?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.360
Take these.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.170
What are they?

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.430
They contain something micro-sized that will

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:23.060
help support your strength of "heart," 
rendered into a soup-like state.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.620
I call it Micross.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:26.770
Now then!

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.490
It's been a while. Allow me to explain.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:34.320
In short, this receptacle is 
packed full of us nanomachines.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:41.290
If Mavis-dono drinks it, we will be able 
to enhance her body as if by magic.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:41.950
However!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.360
It takes a heavy toll on the body.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.580
So, after I made it, I hesitated over 
whether I should give it to you or not.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.500
If the time comes, please use it.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.960
But even if you do, you can't 
take more than one at a time.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.560
Please limit it to one a day.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.490
Understood.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:03.300
They're coming!

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.580
Three hundred meters ahead! Eight of them!

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.340
They're coming straight for us!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.190
They're probably allies of whatever 
was spying on us yesterday.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:13.830
They seem human, but their speed is inhuman.

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:14.820
Two hundred meters!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.260
A melee fight would be disadvantageous for us.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.170
We'll keep walking as though we are unaware,

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.620
and when they spring their ambush,
 we'll counterattack.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.410
They've split into two groups.
 Watch your backs.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.410
Earth Pillar!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.580
Water Spear!

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.250
Stop right there!

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.520
B-Beastpeople?

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.690
What? They're just kids!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.300
Lay down your weapons!

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.760
Don't resist, and we won't hurt you.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.630
And just so you know! 
There's more of us hiding out there!

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.740
There's no way you can beat us!

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:52.960
And let me tell you, if you 
don't resist, we won't kill you.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.400
<i>Switch to Plan B.</i>

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.020
Lay on the ground with your bellies up.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.480
We'll rub them for you.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.610
Trying to mess with us? Who d'you 
think you are, little girl?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.990
I know you want to, but don't kill them!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:08.740
Let's go!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:15.760
Huh?

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:19.710
What?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.230
Run!

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:21.880
Got it!

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:22.950
Huh?

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.970
Hey! You okay?

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:28.470
The beastpeople are retreating.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.660
Okay.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.370
We're up against beastpeople. 
They have an acute sense of smell.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:37.480
We'll use Mile's search magic 
to track them from afar.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.890
Understood!

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:42.590
Earlier, he said, "don't kill them," didn't he?

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:47.160
He did. And he seemed to
want to disarm and capture us.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:51.910
Do you think the investigation team has 
been captured by those beastpeople?

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.660
It's possible.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.290
Okay. Let's go after them.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.630
Wh-What is all this?

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:23.980
Chasing after the beastpeople has 
led us to quite an unusual scene.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.130
What do we do?

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:26.600
Stopping here and taking back

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:31.660
the information that there are beastpeople 
doing something this massive

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.000
is probably the smart thing to do.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.870
But the quest we took on was to 
search for the investigation team.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.410
That's true.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.640
If the investigation team 
is being held there,

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.130
and a large-scale military force comes,

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:48.490
they could be used as hostages, 
or even killed as a warning.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.660
Let's wait for nightfall and do some scouting.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:04.940
It looks like our hunch was right.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.720
What should we do?

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.780
Please, leave it to me.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.460
It really is a splendid thing,
 your sleep magic.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.980
You can use that kind of magic, too?

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:23.130
If we rely on you too much,

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.920
we really will end up good for nothing.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:42.300
Sorry.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.300
Who are you?

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.980
You're the investigation team, right?

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.700
We're Hunters who have been 
charged with finding you.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:55.080
You're still just kids! Why'd you
 take on such a crazy quest?

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:58.410
I'd rather not hear that from a Hunter 
who got himself captured by beastpeople.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.500
For now, let's get you out of here!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:04.250
Please, wait! Please rescue the professor, too!

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:07.090
Huh? You're not the scholar?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.920
I'm just the assistant.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.660
Yesterday, when they found out 
the professor was a scholar,

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.680
the beastpeople took her to the ruins.

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:18.440
By "ruins," you mean ancient buildings, right?

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.180
Is that what the beastpeople are digging up?

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.690
Let's leave the beastpeople's 
objectives aside for the moment.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:27.560
Right now, we have to free 
the investigation team.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.190
That includes the professor.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:32.440
That's crazy. You're saying you 
can fight the beastpeople?

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:35.600
Their physical abilities are far 
greater than those of humans.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.490
There's no way fledglings 
like you could beat—

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.750
Step away from the bars.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:51.590
Escaping through here, rather than out 
the front, will be less noticeable. Right?

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:55.850
And, just so you know, 
I'm the weakest among us.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.320
You should escape first.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:03.860
We'll save the professor, 
and then meet up with you.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.360
G-Got it.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.000
What's this? Why are there humans here?

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.870
I-It's you!

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:24.840
I thought you looked familiar.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.790
Well, if it isn't the beastpeople 
we met this morning?

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.960
Keep your guard up! 
They aren't ordinary people.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.430
We're in a hurry this time, 
so we'll go with Plan Z.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:36.670
"Full speed. Full power. 
Incapacitate the enemy." Right?

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:37.350
Understood!

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:40.310
Which means this is the 
moment to use this, right?

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.100
I'm counting on you, Micross!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.520
Godspeed Sword! 1.5x speed!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.490
Sh-She's fast!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.280
Are you really human?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.380
Amazing! This power-up is unbelievable!

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:58.230
The strength is just welling up inside me!

00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.950
Flame Sphere, continuous fire!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.460
Ultra Hot Water Current!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.460
Um, I don't have any particular 
name for this skill...

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:18.310
You took the professor, right?

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.330
Where did you take her?

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.600
Deep in the ruins.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.800
But it would be better not to go.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.040
Why?

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.350
You won't come back alive.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.230
What a clichéd threat.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.440
If that's what you think, 
then go ahead and go.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:37.950
Wh-What is all this?

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.300
Is it some kind of altar?

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.790
Maybe the beastpeople are 
worshiping some kind of god?

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:49.780
Look! There's writing, and carvings,
 on part of the wall.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:52.300
I don't recognize the writing.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.670
And I can't tell what the carvings represent.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.750
The images are quite fantastical.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:18:00.510
But seeing them on this huge 
wall makes quite the impression.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.400
I've never seen anything like this.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:09.690
Is it a world someone dreamed up?

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.110
They aren't just imaginings.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:16.650
Maybe someone felt the need to set these
 images down in their life after death.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.510
So, devoting great effort and a tremendous 
amount of time to the endeavor,

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.280
they created this.

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.320
You're the professor, right?

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:25.450
We accepted a quest from the Guild,
 and came to save you.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.650
What? A child?

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.200
Are you okay?

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.230
Thank you.

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.070
How did you guys get in here?

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.670
What about the beastperson guards?

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:39.930
Don't tell me you...

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.260
They really are cruel, 
locking up a child like this.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.920
I'm not a child!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.980
You're humans, right? In that case,
 I'm much older than you.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:49.790
Huh?

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.000
A dwarf?

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.110
I'm an elf!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.730
Then, does that mean you're the scholar?

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.080
That's right.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:58.860
Cu Leleia.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:18:59.650
Nice to meet you.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.970
Well, I'm glad we found you.

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.800
We came to rescue you. Let's go!

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.910
I'm sorry to say this when you've 
taken the trouble to come help me,

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.300
but that won't be possible.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.040
What?

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.480
No one can escape from here.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.050
The beastpeople aren't the 
ones who rule this place.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.870
A-An earth dragon?

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:29.000
So this is the cause of the 
strange phenomena in the forest.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.530
It doesn't seem like it's 
going to let us escape.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:33.940
Cu Leleia-san, please stay back.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.190
Wait! All of you!

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.700
Godspeed Sword!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.080
Flame Sphere!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.540
Water Ball! Ultra Hot!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.320
You're kidding!

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:55.250
It can't be!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.460
What's going on?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:58.640
Please, leave it to me!

00:19:58.640 --> 00:19:59.980
Explosion Magic!

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:03.250
Shoot!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:06.740
Huh?

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:11.230
Hmph. Impressive magic, for humans.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.050
I-It talks?

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:15.610
It's no earth dragon.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.860
It's the strongest monster in 
the world. An elder dragon!

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:20.360
Mile! Run!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.750
Mile!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.900
M... Mile?

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.840
When the moment of death arrives, you die.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.840
Truly. Just like that.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.170
She's not dead.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.850
Mile wouldn't die!

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:57.610
We won't let her die!

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:00.980
She's already died.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.210
She's not dead!

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:06.360
It takes a heavy toll on the body.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.280
Please, limit it to one a day.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.240
And what of it?

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:13.500
If I don't use them now, when will I?

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.920
Extra Godspeed Sword! 1.5x speed!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.340
Maximum Flame Sphere!

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:31.350
Zero-Zero Magic No. 1! Rock Reveal!

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:39.770
Impressive, managing to scratch me.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:42.040
You're very good.

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:43.480
How interesting...

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:54.250
<i>No matter what it takes...</i>

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:56.410
<i>Until Mile-chan recovers...</i>

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:58.670
<i>We three will protect her!</i>

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:05.050
I am not an opponent you 
could ever hope to defeat.

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:13.100
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
